# The engine links the ROCm runtime by soname and carries no RUNPATH:
#
#   readelf -d /usr/bin/gufo | grep -E 'RPATH|RUNPATH'      -> nothing
#
# /etc/ld.so.conf.d/rocm.conf therefore has to reach the dynamic linker, and for a
# non-standard directory the cache has to be rebuilt or the library is simply not found:
#
#   /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --inhibit-cache --library-path /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu /usr/bin/gufo --version
#     -> error while loading shared libraries: libhipblas.so.3
#
# This package ships no maintainer script to do it, which is the point: libc-bin declares
# `interest-await ldconfig`, so activating that trigger makes libc-bin refresh the cache as
# part of the same transaction. Proven in debian:trixie against the negative control, payload
# identical in shape (a conf file plus a library in a non-standard directory), each run on a
# pristine container:
#
#   without this file : conf installed, no trigger line, cache not refreshed, lib not indexed
#   with this file    : "Processing triggers for libc-bin", cache refreshed, lib indexed
#
# If a future change moves /opt/rocm off this line, this trigger is what has to move with it.
activate ldconfig
